                        "entry_id": "cec5842a-8d7d-3691-877c-319f51f498ae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A man whose spouse has died (and who has not remarried); a man in relation to his late spouse; masculine of widow."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d56fc04-c76a-4e12-b20d-c9779d9413d9",
                                "sense_id": "a34c2815-a560-31f8-932e-c998cda2eb71",
                                "text": "Tears of the widower, when he sees\n⁠A late-lost form that sleep reveals,\n⁠And moves his doubtful arms, and feels\nHer place is empty, fall like these; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ffbc27d-0b88-4270-805a-645956efeede",
                                "sense_id": "a34c2815-a560-31f8-932e-c998cda2eb71",
                                "text": "What happens to the lovers of people with AIDS? How do they experience the passage from lover to caregiver to \"widower\"?"
                            }
                        ]
